{"base_rate":0.5376486129458389,"brier":0.19878110964332896,"bss":0.20034176131976122,"bss_hi":0.28978040501371705,"bss_lo":0.09660938679503914,"chart":{"base":[526.8,191.1],"fp":[396.8,204.4],"lead":"62,270.2 272,251.9 482,221.7 692,174.7","note":{"base":"skill 0.20 — higher than 27% of cities","fp":"low end +12pp, high end +18pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 80% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 12%; promised 99% → rained 78%"},"rel":"64.6,415.4 205.5,315.6 531.9,184.1 684.4,130.6"},"country":"IE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.15166446499339498,"ess":331.6456970115319,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Dublin</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Dublin rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 6 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>84%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>12%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nDUBLIN PHOENIX PARK, 5.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.20, ranked 157 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(105&ndash;178) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>145</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>23%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'><b>47%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>63%</td><td class='num'><b>55%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>85%</td><td class='num'><b>74%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>95%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>84%</b></td><td class='num'>232</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">6 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Dublin</b> <span class=\"muted\">Ireland</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;54% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 54% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">6 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.20</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>105&ndash;178\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Dublin &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Dublin\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.440413793103446,376.9793103448276 99.57341463414633,315.4146341463415 180.82868421052632,214.3684210526316 282.39373134328355,110.35820895522386 357.9432432432433,47.51351351351349 396.0044444444444,18.0 411.8321551724138,18.0 411.8321551724138,19.568965517241395 396.0044444444444,53.950617283950635 357.9432432432433,101.62162162162161 282.39373134328355,197.28358208955223 180.82868421052632,295.7894736842105 99.57341463414633,364.2439024390244 59.440413793103446,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"186.29590488771464\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"186.29590488771464\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.440413793103446,339.3241379310345 99.57341463414633,297.6585365853658 180.82868421052632,209.57894736842107 282.39373134328355,180.98507462686567 357.9432432432433,111.45945945945948 396.0044444444444,166.2962962962963 411.8321551724138,76.05172413793105\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 12% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 145 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.440413793103446\" cy=\"339.3241379310345\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 12%&amp;#10;It rained 23% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 82 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"99.57341463414633\" cy=\"297.6585365853658\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 35%&amp;#10;It rained 47% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"180.82868421052632\" cy=\"209.57894736842107\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 63%&amp;#10;It rained 55% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"282.39373134328355\" cy=\"180.98507462686567\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 74% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"357.9432432432433\" cy=\"111.45945945945948\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 95%&amp;#10;It rained 59% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"396.0044444444444\" cy=\"166.2962962962963\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 84% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 232 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.8321551724138\" cy=\"76.05172413793105\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(54%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Dublin the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.29) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.02).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'>0.016</td><td class='num'>18.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>59%</td><td class='num'>0.153</td><td class='num'>13.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'>0.217</td><td class='num'>13.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>68%</td><td class='num'>0.286</td><td class='num'>15.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":53.33306,"lon":-6.24889,"n":757,"n_cities":216,"name":"Dublin","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.00406896551724138,"n":145,"obs":0.11724137931034483,"sig":true},{"hi":0.2380000000000004,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.1174390243902439,"n":82,"obs":0.23170731707317074,"sig":true},{"hi":0.4740000000000003,"lo":0.2380000000000004,"mean":0.34697368421052627,"n":76,"obs":0.47368421052631576,"sig":true},{"hi":0.78,"lo":0.4740000000000003,"mean":0.6338805970149254,"n":67,"obs":0.5522388059701493,"sig":false},{"hi":0.92,"lo":0.78,"mean":0.8472972972972973,"n":74,"obs":0.7432432432432432,"sig":true},{"hi":0.99,"lo":0.92,"mean":0.9548148148148147,"n":81,"obs":0.5925925925925926,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.99,"mean":0.9995258620689655,"n":232,"obs":0.8405172413793104,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.8,"provisional":false,"rank":157,"rank_hi":178.0,"rank_lo":105.0,"reliability":0.028915852591383646